          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for to regard as, then the Telugu for an angle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: వాదన",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వాదన — vādana — \"a line of reasoning; an argument\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అతని వాదనలో బలం లేదు. atani vādanalō balaṁ lēdu. There is no strength in his argument."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: వాదనలు, vādanalu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The case you make, not a quarrel. Its verb is వాదించు, to argue, which you know."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వాదన (vādana) is built on Sanskrit vāda, \"speech, statement\" (CDIAL 11507), from the root vad, \"to speak\"; the verb వాదించు comes from the same word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
