          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నిరూపించు — nirūpiñcu — \"to prove\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆమె తన మాట నిజమని నిరూపించింది. āme tana māṭa nijamani nirūpiñcindi. She proved that what she said was true."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): నిరూపించాను, nirūpiñcānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What you prove is often a clause ending in అని:... నిజమని నిరూపించు (nirūpiñcu), to prove that... is true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నిరూపించు (nirūpiñcu) is built on Sanskrit nirūpaṇa, \"stating, determining, defining\", and also \"examination\" (Monier-Williams), with the Telugu verb ending -ఇంచు."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
