          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సహేతుకమైన — sahētukamaina — \"reasonable; well-grounded\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అది సహేతుకమైన ప్రశ్న. adi sahētukamaina praśna. That is a reasonable question."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A reason stands behind it: స-, with, + హేతు, a reason. The ending -మైన makes an adjective, as in కఠినమైన."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సహేతుకమైన (sahētukamaina) is built on Sanskrit sahetuka, \"together with a reason\" (Monier-Williams), from sa-, \"with\", and hetu, \"a cause, a reason\"; Telugu adds -మైన to make an adjective."
            }
          ]
        },
